"""ffx - the package author's tool for ForgeFIRM extension packages.

    ffx new DIR --id ID --runtime ui|python|shell|native|data [--name NAME] [--key NAME.pub]
    ffx lint DIR
    ffx pack DIR [--key KEY.priv] [--out FILE]
    ffx keygen NAME
    ffx install FILE --machine ADDR [--user NAME] [--grant CAPABILITY]...
    ffx logs --machine ADDR [--user NAME] [--id ID] [--follow]
    ffx index record FILE.ffx --url URL [--key AUTHOR.pub | --official-key OPENGLOW.pub] [--out FILE]
    ffx index build CATALOG --version V [--key KEY.priv] --out FILE

`lint` judges a package the way the machine's extension host does, in its
words, and stops where it would: the manifest, the capabilities, the page,
the service's entry point, the payload's limits, and a Python package's
imports against the release image's module list. `pack` lints, then builds
the archive with fwup (the same one a machine verifies with), signs it when
given a key, and checks the signature before it says so. `install` logs in
to a machine over HTTPS, uploads, shows what the machine says the package is
and asks for, and installs with the consent its tier takes. `logs` reads the
extension host's log, a package's lines alone with --id. `index record` and
`index build` are OpenGlow's: a listed version's record from its signed
archive, and the signed index of the catalog from those records.

Extension API 0.1. Python 3.8 or later and the standard library; fwup for
pack and keygen (set FWUP to its path).
"""
